# The CONCEPT DOI, which resolves to the newest release; the per-version DOI of
# 1.0.0 is 10.5281/zenodo.23105029 and freezes on that one release. Safe to keep
# here across future releases: Zenodo's CFF reader (zenodo-rdm, github/schemas.py)
# loads title, abstract, authors, keywords, license and message only — it has no
# handling for `doi` at all, so this field feeds GitHub's "Cite this repository"
# and nothing else. Do not swap it for the version DOI, which goes stale on the
# next release.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23105028"
repository-code: "https://github.com/BulyK47/mee-app"
abstract: >-
  A bilingual (Romanian/English) progressive web application that teaches the
  university course "Măsurări Electrice și Electronice" through short,
  gamified lessons. The design combines a Duolingo-style lesson ladder with a
  domain-specific twist: every figure is a parametric SVG instrument rendered
  from the exercise data (analog meters, oscilloscope screens, bridges,
  wattmeter connections, operational-amplifier configurations), formulas are
  typeset natively with MathML, and progress is rewarded with instruments for
  a virtual laboratory bench. It also includes spaced repetition of mistakes
  and an exam simulation mode. The question bank itself is not distributed.
keywords:
  - engineering education
  - gamification
  - electrical measurements
  - progressive web app
  - spaced repetition
  - bilingual learning
# ONE licence, deliberately, even though three instructional content files are
# dual-licensed under CC BY 4.0 as well — that is documented in NOTICE and in
# README, both of which travel inside the Zenodo archive.
#
# A list here is valid CFF 1.2.0 and passes every offline validator, but Zenodo
# implements only a subset: its schema declares license as a single string, so
# an array raises a validation error, the GitHub release is marked FAILED and
# no DOI is issued at all. The error it shows is "Citation metadata load
# failed", which names nothing. See zenodo/zenodo#2515 — open since 2023.
# Recovery would mean deleting the release and the tag and starting again.
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-02"
